WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
Beijing gets less than 100 cubic metres
of water per person a year from its own

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.330
area.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.230
That's a twentieth of China's average,
and an eightieth of the world's.

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.610
Satellites show water storage falling in
North China and rising in South China.

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.230
In 2002, China launched the
South-North Water Transfer.

6
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.410
Since December 2014, water from the
Danjiangkou Reservoir has flowed north to

7
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:26.750
Beijing.

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.250
But is moving a river really the answer?

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.790
In this mission, you'll trace the central
route and see how Beijing used its new

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.730
water.

11
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.590
Then you'll weigh its advantages
against its disadvantages.

12
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: decide whether moving a river
is the answer to Beijing's water shortage.
